ediate"><addressbook><name>UCHIYAMA, AKIHIKO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAHATA, KAZUO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KON TATSUICHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KUSHIDA TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UCHIYAMA AKIHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAHATA KAZUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KON, TATSUICHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KUSHIDA, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UCHIYAMA, AKIHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAHATA, KAZUO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A liquid crystal display having an improved light use efficiency, and a light source constituting the liquid crystal display. This display comprises (I) a light source for emanating a linearly polarized light having one vibrational direction including (i) a light guide made of a transparent medium and having an end face on which a light from a light source falls, two faces opposed to each other and one acting as an output face, and a haze-anisotropic layer, (ii) a light source disposed on the end face of the optical guide, and (iii) a reflector disposed near the face opposed to the output face of the optical guide; and (II) a polarizer disposed on the output face side of the optical guide such that the axis of polarization is parallel with the direction in which the haze value in the haze-anisotropic layer takes the maximum.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention concerne un affichage à cristaux liquides où l'utilisation de la lumière est plus efficace, ainsi qu'une source de lumière faisant partie de cet affichage à cristaux liquides. L'affichage à cristaux liquides comprend (I) une source de lumière permettant d'émettre une lumière polarisée linéairement et ayant une seule direction vibratoire, laquelle source comprend: (i) un guide de lumière qui est fait d'un matériau transparent et qui comprend une face d'extrémité que vient heurter la lumière provenant d'une source de lumière, deux faces opposées dont l'une sert de face de sortie, et une couche anisotropique au brouillard; (ii) une source de lumière disposée sur la face d'extrémité du guide optique; et (iii) un réflecteur disposé à proximité de la face du guide optique qui est opposée à la face de sortie. L'affichage à cristaux liquides comprend également (II) un polariseur disposé du côté de la face de sortie du guide optique de sorte que l'axe de polarisation soit parallèle à la direction dans laquelle la valeur de brouillard, dans la couche anisotropique au brouillard, est maximale.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>